1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,497
In 1939,

2
00:00:00,497 --> 00:00:03,168
UC Berkeley graduate student George Dantzig

3
00:00:03,168 --> 00:00:05,716
walked late into Professor Jerzy Neyman's

4
00:00:05,716 --> 00:00:06,772
statistics class,

5
00:00:06,772 --> 00:00:09,195
copied two famous unsolved theorems off

6
00:00:09,195 --> 00:00:11,866
